invariant: INV-26
file: record.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: the record layer seals an AES-GCM record through gcm_seal, the
  public-key entry, with a cast that silences the compiler, so a traffic
  key from the TLS key schedule reaches an entry INV-26 keeps for the
  three public keys RFC 9001 fixes. In an AES=soft object that entry is
  the S-box indexed with the key. The two key types are what refuse this
  edit without the cast; with it, inv-26-aes-public-keys-only is what
  fails, because record.c may name the traffic families and nothing else,
  and it can: record.c's seal and open bodies are written so the rule's C
  parser reads them.

--- old
    gcm_traffic_seal(&k, nonce, hdr, REC_HDR, body, len, body, body + len);
--- new
    gcm_seal((const aes_public_key *)(const void *)&k, nonce, hdr, REC_HDR, body, len, body,
             body + len);
